  "worked_solution": "Let's simplify the expression by factoring both the numerator and the denominator:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3{x}^{2}-9x}{4x-12} & =\\frac{3x(x-3)}{4(x-3)}=\\frac{3x}{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the denominator is never zero, we conclude that this function has no vertical asymptotes. A plot of the function is below. Note that it is not defined at $x=3.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979852/assets/d1f0db6bba6e5bbd0079ae06a9f5199eaf8f24c4dfe0890ee691e2a5afcafc30.png)",
